From 4c5e76e974db7cca853619ca138eecd8f004622f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Teguh Sobirin <teguh@sobir.in>
Date: Mon, 27 Oct 2025 16:51:01 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: Add panel driver for Chipone ICNA35XX based panels

Signed-off-by: Teguh Sobirin <teguh@sobir.in>

Folded in on top of the original driver, by virtudude <virtudude@protonmail.com>:
a luminance-linear sysfs backlight scale. Both DDICs drive their panels at
luminance ~ (DBV/4096)^2.2, measured on the AYN Odin 3 (ICNA3520) and Odin 2
Portal (ICNA3512) modules, so raw DBV in sysfs compresses the useful range
into the top of the scale and collapses the low end under nits-based
brightness control. Writes are translated through the brightness levels
helper (0480-drm-panel-add-brightness-levels-helper.patch) and the backlight
declares BACKLIGHT_SCALE_LINEAR.

The shared icna35xx table ends at 3413, the DBV ceiling the vendor Android
trees set for those modules, rather than 4096, which is one past the 12-bit
register. The DDIC does not enforce the ceiling: on the Odin 3, white-screen
panel power at DBV 4095 is 73% above DBV 3413. The sysfs range stays 0..4096,
so userspace is unaffected. The levels are the analytic response
round(round(4096 * (i/128)^(1/2.2)) * ceiling / 4096) -- the 2.2 exponent is a
property of the DDIC family (one table already serves both ICNA3512 and
ICNA3520) and the ceiling is the only per-module input.

Also folded in: the MANGMI Pocket Max (SM8250), which drives a 1080x1920 DSC
panel on the same DDIC with its own init sequence, a 60/90/120/144 Hz mode
list and a 3515 DBV ceiling. Its timings, DSC parameters and ceiling are
transcribed from the stock Android panel node
qcom,mdss_dsi_ican3512_1080p_7inch_cmd ("7inch" is vendor copy-paste; the
panel is 1080x1920). That node also sets qcom,mdss-dsi-bl-inverted-dbv, which
makes the vendor write DBV MSB-first -- the same byte order as
mipi_dsi_dcs_set_display_brightness_large(). Its levels are the family curve
at 3515: the exponent is inherited, not measured on a Pocket Max, and the
stock firmware records no DBV-to-nits mapping to check it against. Replace the
table if the module is ever measured, or override per-board with
brightness-levels in the panel node.

A desc naming no levels table would fail drm_panel_bl_levels_init() and leave
that panel dark, so every desc must carry one.

Also folded in, from gennro (Kettle Linux): no backlight DSI traffic while
the panel is off. A failed init sequence in prepare cut the supplies with
the panel out of reset; it now asserts reset first, as unprepare does.
update_status cleared MIPI_DSI_MODE_LPM and set it back only on success; it
now restores it either way. Brightness writes went over DSI while the panel
was unprepared (no supplies, the DSI host possibly off); they are skipped
then, since drm_panel_enable() calls backlight_enable(), which sends the
brightness once the panel is up. And .get_brightness is gone: it read the
DBV back over DSI at every read of actual_brightness, also while the panel
was off, and reported it unmapped, a different scale from the
luminance-linear sysfs value (the helper has no inverse). The backlight
core now reports the set value.

Rebased onto 7.3, which merged an earlier version of this same driver
(f747473a838e: four per-board compatibles, a single 165 Hz mode, no levels
table, no Mangmi). This patch is now that upstream file -> our fork, .c
only: the Kconfig entry (byte-identical) and the Makefile line are
upstream's. The file it produces is byte-identical to what the 7.2 stack
produced, so 0531-0534 apply on exactly the code they were written against.
